  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Define a versioned support matrix covering accepted resources/envelopes, exact base/profile expectations, bundle/reference rules, element and extension handling, terminology policy, and explicit additional-resource decisions.",
    "Provide consistent machine-readable profile and validation artifacts without inventing payer-specific semantics.",
    "Provide deterministic structured validation for JSON/base structure, profile compatibility, bundle/reference integrity, project invariants, unsupported content, and provenance/data-classification gates.",
    "Inventory the unchanged four-file seed corpus with immutable identifiers, observed facts, approved synthetic-local classification, and honest provenance/license limitations; accept it only when the project-defined minimal FHIR R4 compatibility rules pass.",
    "Treat checksum-pinned CARIN 2.2.0 validation as advisory diagnostics: preserve errors and warnings as structured evidence, never claim CARIN conformance when errors exist, and never allow CARIN results to override project acceptance or rejection.",
    "Preserve unavailable terminology systems and codes as opaque source data with terminology-unverified status; do not substitute terminology, assert membership, or use unverified values independently for coverage, payment, coding, fraud, clinical, or policy conclusions.",
    "Add only clearly project-authored synthetic negative, boundary, and adversarial fixtures outside dataset/ with lineage and coverage for malformed JSON, prohibited classification, broken references, missing required fields, unsupported resources/profiles/envelopes, active content, and invariant cases.",
    "Provide a pinned offline validation procedure that distinguishes minimal-profile-valid, carin-nonconformant, terminology-unverified, and rejected; proves failures are fail-closed; and verifies dataset/ remains byte-identical without network, cloud, model, production, or live terminology-service access.",
    "Distinguish FHIR conformance from coverage, payment, coding, fraud, clinical, and policy correctness, leaving undeclared semantics unsupported.",
    "Document stable downstream handoffs, deferred decisions, versioning triggers, and required architecture or contract review for later changes."
  ],
  "created_by": "human"
